# ============================================================================
# 04_ Multi-task elastic net: NEPC_score + ASPC_fraction — v2
# ============================================================================
# Consumes the single-cell derived feature sets from 02_ and 03_, and writes
# the coefficient / stability tables that 06_ integrates.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE BUG THAT MOTIVATED v2
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1's "PATCH Fix A" claimed to restrict the model to `aspc_features_bulk`:
#
#     aspc_features_bulk <- intersect(rownames(logCPM), colnames(datExpr))
#     datExpr <- datExpr[, aspc_features_bulk, drop = FALSE]
#
# `datExpr` was built as `t(logCPM)`, so `colnames(datExpr)` IS
# `rownames(logCPM)`. The intersect returns everything and the subset is a
# NO-OP. The model was still fitted on all ~5,000 top-variance genes, not on
# the ASPC feature set. Every downstream claim about "ASPC features" was
# therefore unsupported.
#
# v2 defines aspc_features_bulk from the ACTUAL single-cell evidence:
#     tau_<group>_all_datasets.csv     (02_)  — cluster specificity
#     ratio_<group>_all_datasets.csv   (03_)  — target-cluster enrichment
#     target_markers_<group>_recurrence.csv (03_) — cross-cohort recurrence
# and intersects that with the genes measured in the bulk cohort.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OTHER CHANGES IN v2
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   * Paths corrected to /Volumes/Jingjing_Chen (v1 used "Jingjing Chen").
#   * Stability selection now run for BOTH targets. v1 bootstrapped only
#     NEPC_score, then wrote a single `stability_freq` column that 06_ would
#     apply to ASPC genes as though it described them.
#   * Residualisation vectorised via a single QR solve instead of a per-gene
#     lm.fit loop (~5,000 iterations).
#   * alpha is now tuned over a grid rather than fixed at 0.5.
#   * Feature-set provenance written to aspc_features_bulk.csv so the gene
#     universe used by the models is auditable.
#   * Guards added for n_samples < n_features and for degenerate targets.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OUTPUTS (out_dir)
#   multi_task_coefficients.csv   gene, coef_NEPC_like, coef_ASPC_fraction,
#                                 multi_task_positive          <- 06_ reads
#   stability_selection.csv       gene, stability_freq, stability_freq_aspc,
#                                 stability_selected           <- 06_ reads
#   aspc_features_bulk.csv        the feature universe + why each gene is in it
#   model_diagnostics.csv         per-target lambda, alpha, CV error, n_nonzero
#   nepc_score_per_sample.csv     the computed NEPC score, for inspection
# ============================================================================

